        description
            Deliverable: Add one packed-consumer integration matrix across accepted public routes,
            production hosts and Runtime, operation families, and artifact owners.
            Use existing owner proofs for semantics; add only reachability and distinct failure
            scenarios. Return product gaps to their owning phase Tasks.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/test/packed/** and
            reference/incident-console/implementation/test/everclear-new-intent/**.
            Evidence: Fresh packed bootstrap and quickstart readiness, separate API-P03 production
            actor-turn proof, owner-lease disposal, persistence restoration, isolated request
            Runtime, Story/model parity, operation and lifecycle reachability, ordered disposal
            evidence, and T604's installed CLI parity.
        acceptance
            Record one crosswalk row per satisfied outcome below. Each row names its production
            owner Tasks, exact source proof ID/path and command/result, and distinct packed
            scenario.
            PublicSurface.O2 — P1 T002/T004/T008; packed definition and machine consumer through
            AMEND-API-001 readiness, proved by AMEND-P05. The quickstart is not the production
            actor-turn proof.
            PublicSurface.O3 — P1 T005; P3 T300-T305; packed canonical resource and transaction
            turn.
            PublicSurface.O4 — P1 T006/T007; P2 T255/T270; P5 T500; lease-backed React host.
            PublicSurface.O5 — P5 T501-T503; packed Story commands, TestClock, and live model
            parity.
            PublicSurface.O6 — P4 T403/T404; P5 T504/T505; T604; inspect artifact and CLI parity.
            Hosts.O1 — P2 T270; P4 T401/T402; P5 T501; pure detached preparation, then
            Implementation acquisition, then actor/Store installation. Check closed App.M,
            context refs, sealing, activation, no early handles, and failed boot rollback.
            Hosts.O2 — P2 T255/T269/T270; P5 T500; stable/local refs, exact owner lease,
            tombstone, foreign lookup, and dependent blocking.
            Hosts.O4 — P2 T270; P4 T400-T402; P5 T500; inert SSR, isolated persisted request
            Runtimes, and request-owner cleanup.
            Hosts.O5 — P2 T254/T269/T270; P4 T404; P5 T500-T502; reverse cleanup drains
            finalizers and accepted evidence before sink close.
            Runtime.O1 — P1 T002/T004/T009; API-P03 separately proves a packed authored event
            reaches one production turn.
            Runtime.O2 — P1 T006; P2 T202/T270; closed App.M admission rejects foreign identity.
            Runtime.O3 — P2 T254/T270; P4 T401; ready barrier blocks handles and rolls back
            failed boot.
            Runtime.O4 — P2 T269; P3 T301-T305; packed turn publishes one actor/store cut.
            Runtime.O5 — P2 T255/T257/T265-T270; P5 T500; provider suspension and lease cleanup.
            Runtime.O6 — P4 T402/T404; P5 T501-T503; Story capture and live model parity.
            Operations.O1 — P3 T300/T301/T302/T303/T305; descriptor/K sharing, owned P,
            read/write, commit/rollback, affected-actor fanout, Runtime isolation.
            Operations.O3 — P3 T301/T303/T304; changed binding releases once, stream/activity
            cancellation finalizes before resume, timer replacement fences stale completion.
            Operations.O4 — P3 T301-T304; passive packed reader starts no operation work.
            Artifacts.O1 — P4 T400/T402; absent provider does no I/O; scoped setup is inert,
            restore precedes work, writes serialize, and failure keeps the last good record.
            Artifacts.O2 — P4 T401/T402; receiving AppPlan identity/version mismatch rejects;
            provider-first stable restore keeps exact refs/bindings, skips initialization and
            replay.
            Artifacts.O5 — P3 T305; P4 T404; global sequence, bounded sink truncation/clear,
            accepted prefix drain, failure isolation, and no acknowledgment delay.
            Artifacts.O6 — P4 T403/T404; canonical raw round-trip and deterministic exact-path
            redaction preserve raw bytes; share import rejects and does not mutate Runtime truth.
            Verification.O3 — P4 T404; P5 T501-T503; TestClock, checkpoints, failure evidence,
            and production model/live parity.
            Also prove Verification.V3 with P2 T255/T257/T265-T270 and P3 T300-T305:
            one packed descriptor/K retains P through read/write, commit/rollback and fanout,
            fences cancellation, and stays isolated from a second Runtime.
            Each row records the owner proof path/ID and exact check result; source checks alone do
            not count as the packed scenario.
            Use accepted public routes only; deferred routes stay absent until T606 records their
            Workflow owner and route decision. No integration test duplicates an owner's semantic
            matrix. Package promotion remains gated by Cutover.Q1 and T605.
            Run `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types`,
            `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite build`,
            `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:packed-consumers`,
            `nubx vp test packages/flow-state-rewrite`, `nub run lint`, and application-owned
            browser checks. Expected: all checks pass.
